  "dealing": "Dealing",
  "menuForTheFirstDealThePlayerWhoDrewThe": "For the first deal, the player who drew the lowest card deals. They shuffle and have the opponent to their left cut, leaving more than one card above or below the cut. The dealer deals one card at a time from the top, starting with the opponent to their right, who has the lead (Esku). Each player must check how many cards they receive. Players may look at their cards before the deal is complete.",
  "menuIfACardIsTurnedOverDuringTheFirst": "If a card is turned over during the first deal, or any other irregularity occurs (more or fewer than 4 cards, etc.), collect all cards, shuffle, cut and deal again.",
  "menuIfTheErrorIsFoundAfterPlayHasBegun": "If the error is found after play has begun, meaning after a player has stopped the Mus, the player with more or fewer than four cards does not take part and their team’s points are cancelled.",
  "menuIfACardIsTurnedOverAfterMusHas": "If a card is turned over after Mus has been agreed once, play continues normally.",
  "menuEskuAndTheirPartnerDecideWhetherToStopWith": "Esku and their partner decide whether to stop with Mintza or choose Mus by saying Zuetan or “Over to you”. Their opponents then do the same in turn.",
  "menuIfThereIsMusAll4PlayersDiscardThe": "If there is Mus, all 4 players discard the desired number of cards at once, with ESKU first. The dealer then gives each player their replacement cards in one batch.",
  "menuPlayBeginsWithESKUFirstHighThenLowPairs": "Play begins with ESKU first: High, then Low, Pairs, Game or Point. Biak Embido and Biak Hordago bids are permitted.",
  "menuTiraIdukiAndHordagoBindTheTeamTheSpeakers": "Tira, Iduki and Hordago bind the team: the speaker’s partner cannot overrule them, even as Esku. Both Nere gatik tira and Tira nere gatik, or “For me, fold”, leave the partner free to raise. When both partners bet or raise, the first decision stands. After Hordago Kanta, no points (tantto) are scored.",
  "menuSigns": "Signs",
  "menuOnlyTheFollowingOfficialSignsAreAllowed": "Only the following official signs are allowed:",
  "menu2KingsLowerLip": "2 Kings: lower lip.",
  "menu2AcesStickOutTheTongue": "2 Aces: stick out the tongue.",
  "menuMediakMoveOneSideOfTheLips": "Mediak: move one side of the lips.",
  "menuDobliakMoveBothSidesOfTheLips": "Dobliak: move both sides of the lips.",
  "menu29SameAsMediak": "29: same as mediak.",
  "menu30Or31Wink": "30 or 31: wink.",
  "menuGameRaiseTheEyebrows": "Game: raise the eyebrows.",
  "menuTheSignFor30Or31MayBeMade": "The sign for 30 or 31 may be made at any time. The sign for 29 may only be sent after Pairs is over. The Game sign is forbidden with 31.",
  "menuDoublePairs": "Double pairs",
  "menuWhen2OpponentsHaveDoublePairsWithTheSame": "When 2 opponents have double pairs with the same higher pair, the one with the stronger lower pair always wins. Example: two elevens + two sevens beat two elevens + two sixes, even in last position.",
  "menuErrors": "Errors",
  "menuAnnouncingPairsWithoutHavingAny": "Announcing pairs without having any:",
  "menuAIfThePartnerHasNoneAllBetsOn": "a) If the partner has none, all bets on Pairs are cancelled. The opponent still scores the points for their pair or pairs.",
  "menuBIfThePartnerHasPairsAndTheOpponents": "b) If the partner has pairs and the opponents do too, all bets on Pairs are cancelled; the opponent scores the TIRA for Pairs and the points for their pair or pairs.",
  "menuFailingToAnnouncePairsWhenHoldingThem": "Failing to announce pairs when holding them:",
  "menuUnannouncedPairsCannotBeUsedToBetCallOr": "Unannounced pairs cannot be used to bet, call or score later.",
  "menuIfThePartnerHasNoPairsAnOpponentWith": "If the partner has no pairs, an opponent with pairs scores one Tira point.",
  "menuAnnouncingGameWithoutHavingIt": "Announcing Game without having it:",
  "menuAIfNoneOfTheOther3PlayersHas": "a) If none of the other 3 players has Game, the opponents score the Tira for Point and the Pontua point.",
  "menuBIfThePartnerHasGameAndTheOpponents": "b) If the partner has Game and the opponents do not, the error is ignored.",
  "menuCIfThePartnerHasNoGameButAn": "c) If the partner has no Game but an opponent does, Game bets are cancelled and the opponent scores their Game points.",
  "menuDIfThePartnerAndAnOpponentBothHave": "d) If the partner and an opponent both have Game, Game bets are cancelled; the opponent scores the TIRA for Game and their Game points.",
  "menuFailingToAnnounceGameWhenHoldingIt": "Failing to announce Game when holding it:",
  "menuAIfNoneOfTheOther3PlayersHas465": "a) If none of the other 3 players has Game, Point bets are cancelled and the opponent scores the ttantto for Tira and the Pontua point. The unannounced Game does not count.",
  "menuBIfThePartnerHasGameAndTheOpponents466": "b) If the partner has Game and the opponents do not, only the partner’s Game is counted.",
  "menuCIfThePartnerHasNoGameAndAn": "c) If the partner has no Game and an opponent does, that opponent scores the TIRA for Game and their Game points. A player with no pairs or Game cannot bet or raise on behalf of a partner who has them.",
  "menuScoringAndRaises": "Scoring and raises",
  "menuDuringPlayPointsConcededThroughTIRAAreScoredAs": "During play, points conceded through TIRA are scored as they occur. In a perfect tie, ESKU always wins. At the end of each hand, all four players must lay all their cards face up on the table.",
  "menuScoreHighThenLowPairsGameOrPointAs": "Score High, then Low, Pairs, Game or Point as follows:",
  "menuHighIfEveryoneSaidPASOTheBestHighScores": "High: if everyone said PASO, the best High scores 1 point (Haundi Pasa). If High was declined after Embido, nothing is scored. If there was Iduki, only the points bet are scored.",
  "menuLowTheSameAsHigh": "Low: the same as High.",
  "menuPairsAfterPasoTheTeamWithTheBestPair": "Pairs: after Paso, the team with the best pair scores its pairs: 1 point for a pair, 2 for mediak or 3 for double pairs. After Iduki, the bet is added.",
  "menuGameTheSameAsPairsCounting2PointsFor": "Game: the same as Pairs, counting 2 points for Game or 3 for 31, for each Game held by the team that wins Game.",
  "menuPointPontuaAfterPasoTheBestPontuaScores1": "Point (Pontua): after Paso, the best Pontua scores 1 point. After Tira, the team that won the Tira scores 1 Pontua point. After Iduki, the points bet plus 1 Pontua point are scored.",
  "menuRaiseExamples": "Raise examples:",
  "menuEmbido2PointsTira1Point": "Embido (2 points) - Tira = 1 point",
  "menuEmbido2PointsIduki2Points": "Embido (2 points) - Iduki = 2 points",
  "menuHordagoTira1Point": "Hordago - Tira = 1 point",
  "menuHiruEmbido3PointsTira1Point": "Hiru Embido (3 points) - Tira = 1 point",
  "menuHiruEmbido3PointsIduki3Points": "Hiru Embido (3 points) – Iduki = 3 points",
  "menuEmbido2PointsLauGehiago4Tira2Points": "Embido (2 points) Lau gehiago (+ 4) - Tira = 2 points",
  "menuEmbido2PointsBigehiago2HordagoTira4Points": "Embido (2 points) – Bigehiago( +2 ) – Hordago - Tira = 4 points",
  "menuHiruEmbido3PointsLauGehiago4Iduki7": "Hiru Embido (3 points) Lau gehiago (+ 4) Iduki = 7 points",
  "menuEmbido2PointsBortzGehiago5Bigehiago2Tira": "Embido (2 points) Bortz gehiago (+ 5) Bigehiago (+2) Tira = 7 points",
  "menuNoTtanttoMayBeScoredOnceTheCardsHave": "No ttantto may be scored once the cards have been gathered.",
  "menuRefereeing": "Refereeing",
  "menuTheRefereeIntervenesOnlyAtAPlayersRequestOr": "The referee intervenes only at a player’s request or upon observing an irregularity.",
  "menuAnyDisputeOverTheseRegulationsOrAnySituationNot": "Any dispute over these regulations, or any situation not covered here, will be settled by the referee.",
  "menuTheRefereeMayImposePenaltiesUpToAndIncluding": "The referee may impose penalties up to and including exclusion.",
