  "legalTermsBody": "ISAMUS — TERMS OF USE\nDraft dated 26 October 2026 — to be completed before publication\n\nPublisher: [NAME / COMPANY NAME], [ADDRESS], [COUNTRY]. Contact: [SUPPORT EMAIL].\n\n1. The service\nIsaMus lets you play Mus, the 4 Kings / 4 Aces variant, with players or bots. Points and rankings have no monetary value. The service offers neither cash wagers nor winnings exchangeable for money.\n\n2. Account\nA guest account lets you start playing. Linking a verified email address or an Apple/Google identity lets you recover your account. Without this link, losing your session or device may make your progress unrecoverable. Protect your sign-in credentials and choose a respectful nickname that does not disclose personal data.\n\n3. Play and player relationships\nCheating, exploiting vulnerabilities, impersonation, harassment and abusive solicitation are prohibited. Friend requests and invitations may be declined. Bots are identified as such. Disconnections trigger automatic actions so play can continue.\n\n4. Digital items\nCosmetics are visual elements that give no advantage in cards or scores. Items, features and prices are shown before purchase confirmation in the app store. Apple or Google processes payment. IsaMus does not receive your bank card number. Purchases must be linked to a secured account. Restore purchases requests synchronisation. A digital item cannot be converted into money or transferred between players in the app.\nRefund terms and applicable legal rights remain those of your country and app store. Nothing in these terms limits mandatory consumer guarantees. Any information or consent required for immediate delivery of digital content must be provided through the store purchase flow.\n\n5. Advertising\nAds may appear on the home screen. Ad privacy choices are available from your profile. Refusing optional use of your data must not prevent you from playing.\n\n6. Availability and changes\nThe service depends on networks and third-party services. Outages or maintenance may occur. The publisher informs players of significant changes affecting the service or acquired items and respects applicable mandatory rights.\n\n7. Deletion and support\nAccount deletion can be requested in Account & security. It removes the profile and associated data according to the privacy policy. It does not automatically cancel a store transaction. For assistance, contact [SUPPORT EMAIL].\n\n8. Applicable law and disputes\nMandatory consumer protection rules in your place of residence apply. Provisions on applicable law, mediation and the competent authority must be adapted to the publisher’s actual country and status before publication.\n",
  "legalPrivacyBody": "ISAMUS — PRIVACY POLICY\nDraft dated 26 October 2026 — to be completed before publication\n\nData controller: [NAME / COMPANY NAME], [ADDRESS], [COUNTRY]. Contact for your rights: [PRIVACY EMAIL].\n\nData and uses\nYour account has a technical identifier, nickname, Elo rating and statistics. An email address or Apple/Google identity is used only if you choose to secure your account. Sessions authenticate you. Passwords are handled by the authentication service and are not accessible in the app.\nGames contain the participants, actions and states needed to play. History stores results and Elo changes. Friend requests and invitations enable social features. Presence tells accepted friends whether you are online or in a game; it does not reveal the room code.\nYour nickname, avatar and Elo are visible to other authenticated players. Cards and game states are accessible to participants in the current architecture. Do not put sensitive data in your nickname.\n\nPurchases and advertising\nApple/Google stores and RevenueCat handle purchases and validation. Your account identifier and cosmetic access rights allow purchase restoration. We do not collect your bank details.\nWhen advertising is enabled, Google AdMob and its consent mechanism may process technical data about your device, network, ad delivery and privacy choices. The integration requests non-personalised ads; this does not exclude all data processing by the SDK. Applicable consent forms and the Ad privacy choices link let you manage optional uses. The app does not require access to your contacts, microphone or precise location.\n\nGrounds for processing\nOperating the account, game and purchases is based on providing the service you request. Abuse prevention and security are based on the publisher’s legitimate interests, subject to your rights. Optional processing requiring consent must only be enabled after the required choice. Applicable legal obligations may require certain transaction records to be retained.\n\nProviders and transfers\nSupabase provides the database, authentication, server functions and real-time features. Apple, Google and RevenueCat take part in authentication, purchases or advertising depending on the features used. Before publication, the publisher must specify the actual regions, recipients, any international transfers and applicable contractual safeguards; these settings cannot be inferred from the app code.\n\nRetention\nYour profile, inventory and social relationships are kept while your account exists. Presence is linked to your connection. The publisher must document retention periods for history and technical logs: [HISTORY RETENTION], [LOG RETENTION], [BACKUP RETENTION]. Invitations are functionally valid for ten minutes; expiration does not mean immediate deletion from the database. Providers may have their own retention obligations.\n\nYour rights and deletion\nYou may request access, correction, deletion and, where legally applicable, portability, restriction or objection at [PRIVACY EMAIL]. Withdrawing consent does not affect previous lawful processing. Your profile offers account deletion. Requests concerning payments or an advertising identifier may also need to go to the relevant store or provider. You may contact the competent supervisory authority; in France, the CNIL (www.cnil.fr).\n\nMinors\nBefore publication, the publisher must define the minimum age, target audience and any necessary parental consent mechanism. Ad configuration and app store age declarations must reflect this choice.\n\nUpdates\nThe date and significant changes to this policy will be communicated in the app. This draft must be completed with actual publisher and provider information before going online.\n",
